From bce4aef211b3941af9ca297162406fc84f22ed5d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
Date: Thu, 2 Jul 2026 15:09:01 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: mt7915: check default EEPROM firmware size before
 copying

mt7915_eeprom_load_default() copied mt7915_eeprom_size() bytes from the
firmware blob after only checking that it was non-NULL. A truncated
default bin caused an out-of-bounds read past the firmware buffer into
the EEPROM image. Reject a blob smaller than the EEPROM size.

Fixes: beed8bea8d74 ("mt76: mt7915: add mt7916 calibrated data support")
Signed-off-by: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>

Upstream-Status: Backport [bce4aef211b3941af9ca297162406fc84f22ed5d]
OpenWrt-Drop-When: package/kernel/mt76/Makefile PKG_SOURCE_VERSION contains
  bce4aef211b3941af9ca297162406fc84f22ed5d (or an mt76 equivalent of it).
License: BSD-3-Clause-Clear
---
 mt7915/eeprom.c | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

--- a/mt7915/eeprom.c
+++ b/mt7915/eeprom.c
@@ -117,6 +117,12 @@
 		goto out;
 	}
 
+	if (fw->size < mt7915_eeprom_size(dev)) {
+		dev_err(dev->mt76.dev, "Invalid default bin size\n");
+		ret = -EINVAL;
+		goto out;
+	}
+
 	memcpy(eeprom, fw->data, mt7915_eeprom_size(dev));
 	dev->flash_mode = true;
 
